      "paragraphMissing": [
        {
          "text": "To demonstrate streams we will need to use uv_pipe_t. This allows streaming\nlocal files 2. Here is a simple tee utility using libuv.  Doing all operations\nasynchronously shows the power of evented I/O. The two writes won’t block each\nother, but we have to be careful to copy over the buffer data to ensure we don’t\nfree a buffer until it has been written.",
          "source": "guide/filesystem.rst"
        },
        {
          "text": "All modern operating systems provide APIs to put watches on individual files or\ndirectories and be informed when the files are modified. libuv wraps common\nfile change notification libraries 1. This is one of the more\ninconsistent parts of libuv. File change notification systems are themselves\nextremely varied across platforms so getting everything working everywhere is\ndifficult. To demonstrate, I’m going to build a simple utility which runs\na command whenever any of the watched files change:",
          "source": "guide/filesystem.rst"
        }
      ],
