      "paragraphs": 41,
      "paragraphMissing": [
        {
          "text": "It is necessary to set the broadcast flag, otherwise you will get an\nEACCES error 1. The exact message being sent is not relevant to this\nbook and you can study the code if you are interested. As usual the read and\nwrite callbacks will receive a status code of < 0 if something went wrong.",
          "source": "guide/networking.rst"
        },
        {
          "text": "Local loopback of multicast packets is enabled by default 2, use\nuv_udp_set_multicast_loop to switch it off.",
          "source": "guide/networking.rst"
        },
        {
          "text": "libuv provides asynchronous DNS resolution. For this it provides its own\ngetaddrinfo replacement 3. In the callback you can\nperform normal socket operations on the retrieved addresses. Let’s connect to\nLibera.chat to see an example of DNS resolution.",
          "source": "guide/networking.rst"
        }
      ],
