      "paragraphs": 57,
      "paragraphMissing": [
        {
          "text": "Since domain sockets 1 can have a well known name and a location in the\nfile-system they can be used for IPC between unrelated processes. The D-BUS\nsystem used by open source desktop environments uses domain sockets for event\nnotification. Various applications can then react when a contact comes online\nor new hardware is detected. The MySQL server also runs a domain socket on\nwhich clients can interact with it.",
          "source": "guide/processes.rst"
        }
      ],
