        {
          "text": "When using uv_queue_work you’ll usually need to pass complex data through\nto the worker thread. The solution is to use a struct and set\nuv_work_t.data to point to it. A slight variation is to have the\nuv_work_t itself as the first member of this struct (called a baton 1).\nThis allows cleaning up the work request and all the data in one free call.",
          "source": "guide/utilities.rst"
        },
        {
          "text": "You can similarly add more functions that plugin authors can use to do useful\nthings in your application 2. A sample plugin using this API is:",
